<title>CHINA: China's central bank boosts re-discount quota.</title>
<headline>China's central bank boosts re-discount quota.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's central bank plans to boost the quota for re-discounting of bills by 20 billion yuan ($241 million) this year, the official Xinhua news agency said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The news agency said the increase was part of the central bank's plan to foster a domestic market for commercial bank bills and move away from using administrative measures to control money supply.</p>
